    "title_amharic": "መራመድ ሲያቅተው ጓደኞቹ መነኮሳት ተሸክመው ወደ ቤተ ክርስቲያን የወሰዱት መነኩሴ",
    "incipit": "ተብህለ፡ ከመ፡ ሀሎ፡ ፩፡ ደብር፡ ዘመነኮሳት፡ ኀበ፡ ጽንፈ፡ ባሕር። ወሀሎ፡ ውስቴቱ፡ ፩፡ እኅው፡ ዘመንኰሰ፡ እምንእሱ። ወውእቱሰ፡ ብእሲ፡ ሠናይ፡ ውእቱ።",
    "manuscript_count": 295,
    "most_read": false,
    "translations": [
      {
        "author": "Jeremy Brown with Ekaterina Pukhovaia",
        "text": "<p>A miracle performed by Our Lady Mary, Holy Virgin Mariham, the Mother of God, may her intercession be with us, amen.</p>\n\n<p>It is said that there was a monastery for monks near the sea. In it was one brother who had been a monk since his youth. He was a good man: his faith was upright, his fasting and his prayers were numerous, his way of life was good, his heart was pure, and he loved Our Lady Mary, Holy Virgin Mariham, the Mother of Light and the Mother of Mercy. He sweetened the remembrance of her name, he revered Our Compassionate Lady every day, for he was fasting during the day and standing in his duty at night.</p>\n\n<p>Our Lady Mary, the Holy Virgin Mariham, loved him because of his deeds and his good way of life. She wanted to deliver him from the impurities of this world.</p>\n\n<p>A severe illness seized him for many days. He was unable to go to the church, nor to any other place, if the brothers didn’t carry him. When the time of his death drew near, he asked the brothers to carry him and to take him around in front of the altar, so that he might bid them farewell and be blessed by them.</p>\n\n<p>The brothers carried that monk and led him around in front of every altar. He bid them farewell and was blessed by them. After this, they brought him back to his bed, and he praised the brothers.</p>\n\n<p>He said to them, “My dear brothers, may God repay you with every goodness for the toils that you performed on my behalf. I assure you that now I see heaven opened up and Our Lord sitting at the right hand of Power. I also see My Lady Mary Mariham sitting on my right.”</p>\n\n<p>After he said this, his soul departed from his body.</p>\n\n<p>One of the monks was sleeping in his bed at that time. In his sleep, he saw Our Lady Mary, the Holy Pure Virgin Mariham, coming down from heaven. She received the brother who had died and brought him up to heaven.</p>\n\n<p>When that brother [who saw this in his sleep] woke up, he told the other brothers everything he had seen. After they heard this report from him, they marveled and were amazed.</p>\n\n<p>They worshiped the praiseworthy and almighty God, and they praised Our Lady Mary. They knew that the [deceased] brother had been delivered by the intercession of Our Lady Mary, the Holy Virgin Mariham.</p>\n\n<p>Those monks became vigilant and committed to the service of Our Lady Mary Mariham, the Committed, Vigilant, and Aid to those who serve her—the Boat of Life, the Refuge of Salvation.</p>\n\n<p>May the prayer and blessing of Our Lady Mary, the Holy Virgin Mariham, be with your servant Constantine forever and ever, amen, amen, and amen.</p>"
      },
      {
        "author": "Jeremy Brown",
        "text": "<p>A miracle performed by Our Lady Mary, the Holy Twofold Virgin. May her prayer be with her servant Simon forever and ever, amen.</p>\n\n<p>Many monks lived on an island in the middle of the Tigris River called Mount Ephrem.</p>\n\n<p>One of the men among them had been a monk since his youth. He served Our Lady with fine worship. His heart burned with her love. His lips were sweetened by the remembrance of the Virgin’s name, and he was excellent in his good deeds. This monk was a man of God, being devoted to fasting and prayer. He never failed to visit the church of Our Lady Mary. He reverently offered the greeting during the day, and at night he fasted and stood [before her icon].</p>\n\n<p>So Our Lady, the queen of the whole world, accepted him because of his conduct and his fine lifestyle. Because of these things, she prepared deliverance for him from the sin and corruption of this world.</p>\n\n<p>At that time, the monk became sick, and he was unable to travel to the church. He was unable to move about, nor could he walk out of his cell during the time of his want or need.</p>\n\n<p>Instead, [his brother monks] were carried him and placed him where he wanted. Then the illness grew more severe, and he was nearly dead.</p>\n\n<p>So he petitioned his brothers to carry him and to lead him around the area so that he could worship and be blessed by the altar’s tabot.</p>\n\n<p>Then they carried him and led him around. He petitioned and was blessed.</p>\n\n<p>Then they brought him back to his cell, placing him upon his bed. He blessed his brother monks, saying, “My dear brothers, may God finely reward your labors on behalf of my illness, the aid you gave me during my hardship, and the laments you raised with me. Look, I will describe for you [what I see]. I see heaven opened up and Our Lord Jesus Christ sitting at the right hand of the Father. I see Our Lady Mary the Twofold Virgin sitting at the right hand of her beloved son.”</p>\n\n<p>After he said this, the monk died.</p>\n\n<p>One of the monks was sleeping near the monk who had died. And Our Lady Mary announced the good news while descending from heaven in the glory of beautiful light. Then she touched the hand of the monk who had died, and she brought him up to heaven with her with the angels’ jubilant cries. Mary bequeathed to that monk a place of eternal rest and tranquility, where there was delight and enjoyment that never faded away.</p>\n\n<p>When the sleeping monk woke up, he described everything he had seen to his brother monks, and he described how Our Lady had announced the good news to him.</p>\n\n<p>Those who heard this marvelous account were amazed and astonished. They gave worship to God Most High, and they praised Our Lady Mary. They understood with certainty that the pure Virgin had delivered that monk from the hellfire and from the condemnation of the Final Judgment through her petition.</p>\n\n<p>Likewise, may Our Lady guard her servant Simon forever and ever, amen.</p>"
      }
    ]
