    "title": "A monk without food or clothes received a garment from the Virgin Mary",
    "title_amharic": "ልብስና ምግብ ያልነበረው መነኩሴ ከድንግል ማርያም ልብስ ተቀበለ።",
    "incipit": "ተብህለ፡ ከመ፡ ሀሎ፡ ፩መነኮስ፡ ነዳይ፡ ወአልቦቱ፡ አልባስ፡ ወአራዘ፡ ወሲሳየ። ወይትአምና፡ ለእግዝእትነ፡ ቅድስት፡ ድንግል፡ በ፪ኤ፡ ማርያም፡ ማሪሃም፡ ወይቤላ፡ አዝዚ፡ ዘእለብስ፡ ወዘእበልዕ፡ ወዘንተ፡ ብሂሎ፡ ኖመ።",
    "manuscript_count": 247,
    "most_read": false,
    "translations": [
      {
        "author": "Wallis Budge",
        "text": "<p>There was a certain poor monk who had no clothes, no food, and no drink.</p>\n\n<p>He put his trust in Our Lady Mary and said to her, “Give the word that I may eat and have clothes to put on.” Saying this, he went to sleep.</p>\n\n<p>Our Lady Mary came at midnight and made herself appear to him in a vision.</p>\n\n<p>She said, “What do you say, my dear monk? Take this garment to serve you [for clothing].”</p>\n\n<p>He woke from his sleep and found the garment, whereupon he rejoiced greatly.</p>\n\n<p>All those who heard of the miracle that Our Lady Mary had wrought marveled.</p>"
      }
    ]
