    "id": "101",
    "title": "Thieves at the Spring: Part 2: The Virgin Mary saves the soul of a thief who was slain by the miraculous spring",
    "title_amharic": "በምንጭ አጠገብ የተገናኙት ሌቦች፤ ክፍል 4፤ በተአምራዊው ምንጭ አጠገብ የተገደለን ሌባ ነፍስ ድንግል ማርያም ከፍርድ አዳነች።",
    "incipit": "ወእምድኅረ፡ አዕረፈት፡ እግዝእትነ፡ ማርያም፡ መጽአ፡ ካልእ፡ ፋያታይ፡ ኀበ፡ ውእቱ፡ ማይ፡ ዘነቅዓ፡ እምታሕተ፡ እግራ፡ ለማርያም፡ ውዒሎ፡ ኀበ፡ ቀቲለ፡ ነፍስ፡",
    "manuscript_count": 236,
    "most_read": false,
    "translations": [
      {
        "author": "Jeremy Brown & Dawit Muluneh with Wendy Laura Belcher",
        "text": "<p>[So] then, after Our Lady Mary died, another thief, [different from the ones we mentioned previously], came to that water that had sprung up underneath Mary’s feet.</p>\n\n<p>He stayed near the water, [the place] where he had killed someone and shed their blood. He washed off the day’s copious sweat, took a drink, and stepped into the water on top of the stone. After laying down his sword and spear, he fell asleep.</p>\n\n<p>Then, yet another thief came to wash off [in the water]. When he saw the sleeping thief, he drew his sword and cut off the sleeping thief’s head. That thief died a terrible death.</p>\n\n<p>Then, the angels of darkness came and took the dead thief away, [tormenting him by] shaking him.</p>\n\n<p>Then, Mary came, saying, “That soul is mine!”</p>\n\n<p>The angels of darkness responded to her, “This thief didn’t spare the righteous [or the sinner] and he didn’t show mercy to the rich [or the poor].”</p>\n\n<p>Then Mary went [to the divine courtroom] and bowed before Our Lord, saying “My son, show mercy on my behalf. Show mercy on my behalf!”</p>\n\n<p>The Lord said, “The one who is drenched in human blood does not deserve mercy.”</p>\n\n<p>Our Lady Mary replied, “This thief, who cleansed himself in the Garden [of Eden]’s water that you made flow under my feet, has arrived in front of you.”</p>\n\n<p>Then the Lord responded, “[Since] beforehand he cleansed himself in the Garden [of Eden]’s water, which I made flow under your feet, he no longer deserves the judgment of death. Wash him a second time in the water of life and bring him into the Garden [of Eden].”</p>\n\n<p>Then the heavenly hosts bowed down, saying, “Praise be to God, who delights in humanity.”</p>\n\n<p>My dear Lady, may your prayer and petition, and the mercy of your son, be with us, and with your maidservant Batra Aaron, forever and ever and ever, amen.</p>"
      },
      {
        "author": "Wallis Budge",
        "text": "<p>It came to pass after the death of Our Lady Mary that the second thief, after slaying and shedding blood, came to the water that had sprung up under the feet of Our Lady Mary.</p>\n\n<p>He washed away the sweat [caused by] the sun, and he drank. The water washed over the stone [that was] under his head, sword, and spear, and he fell asleep.</p>\n\n<p>[Another] thief came to wash at the spring. When he saw his companion asleep there, he took up his sword and cut off his head. He died immediately.</p>\n\n<p>The angels of darkness came and carried [the murdered thief] away, shaking his soul as they went.</p>\n\n<p>Our Lady Mary came and said, “This soul belongs to me.”</p>\n\n<p>The angels of darkness said to her, “He spared neither the righteous nor the rich.”</p>\n\n<p>Our Lady Mary then went, bowed down before our Lord, and said to him, “Have mercy upon me, my Son; have mercy upon me.”</p>\n\n<p>Our Lord said to her, “Mercy is not fitting for he who is drenched in the blood of men.”</p>\n\n<p>Our Lady Mary said, “He who has washed in the water of the Garden that you caused to spring has come to you.”</p>\n\n<p>The Lord said to her, “The punishment of death is not appropriate for [this man] who has washed in the water of the Garden that I caused to spring up under your feet. Let them wash him again in the water of life and bring him into the Garden [i.e., paradise].”</p>\n\n<p>The hosts of angels prostrated themselves, saying, “Glory be to God, who has pleasure in man.”</p>"
      }
    ]
