    "id": "44",
    "title": "Rizqallah, a priest from Cairo, who vowed to the Virgin Mary that he would stop serving her if she did not help him recover, from Arab thieves, some pilgrims' stolen clothes",
    "title_amharic": "በዐረብ ዘራፊዎች የተወሰደን የመንፈሳዊ ተጓዦች ልብስ ካላስመለስሽ አንቺን ማገልገሌን እተዋለሁ ብሎ ለድንግል ማርያም የማለው ካህኑ ሪዝቃላ",
    "incipit": "ወሀለወት፡ አሐቲ፡ ሀገር፡ በቅሩበ፡ ምስር፡ ምኔት፡ በስመ፡ እግዝእትነ፡ ቅድስት፡ ድንግል፡ ማርያም፡ ዘይሰመይ፡ ደብረ፡ አደውያ። ወያብዕሉ፡ በውስቴታ፡ በዐለ፡ ዐቢየ፡ በስማ፡ ለእግዝእትነ፡ ቅድስት፡ ድንግል፡ ማርያም፡ አመ፡ ፲ወ፯ለነሓሴ፡",
    "manuscript_count": 117,
    "most_read": false,
    "translations": [
      {
        "author": "Jeremy Brown & Dawit Muluneh",
        "text": "<p>The miracle [performed by] Our Lady Mary, Holy Virgin, the Mother of God, may her prayers and blessings be with her servant [King] Lebna Dengel forever and ever. Amen.</p>\n\n<p>A monastery named Dabra Adaweya, dedicated in the name of Our Lady, the Virgin Mary, was located in the vicinity of Egypt. There they would celebrate a great feast in the name of Our Lady, the Holy Virgin Mary, on the sixteenth of Nahase. The nobility of Egypt and [in particular those from] Cairo would come to the monastery and celebrate the festival joyfully.</p>\n\n<p>One year, a priest named Rizqallah was appointed over this [monastery’s] holy church. He was a monk and a lovely chanter, whose house was in Cairo. When the feast of Our Lady Holy Virgin Mary approached on the sixteenth of Nahase, that priest gathered the people, the men and the women, who were adorned with silk and gold garments.</p>\n\n<p>When the monastery’s Arabs saw this, Satan placed an evil thought within their hearts. He counseled them to go to the festival to [steal and] wear their garments and adornments. All of them agreed to Satan’s counsel.</p>\n\n<p>The night before the festival, after completing the evening prayer of incense, all the priests and people went in front of the icon of Our Lady, the Holy Virgin Mary, holding candles and sweet-smelling rose water. They sang in front of the icon, according to their custom.</p>\n\n<p>Having completed the Praise of the Father and the customary chant, they ascended [to the roof] above the upper room to rest. When the Arabs realized [that the priests had gone upstairs], they climbed [up over and] down the walls, going up to them and stealing all their garments and adornments, even the garments of the children. Nothing remained except for a single tunic.</p>\n\n<p>When the priest Rizqallah saw what had happened, he was distressed. He and all the priests descended from [the roof] above the upper room, and they bowed down in front of the icon of Our Lady, the Holy Virgin Mary. Weeping, they begged her to take vengeance against the Arabs who had stolen their possessions.</p>\n\n<p>Rizqallah swore a binding oath in front of the icon of Our Lady, the Holy Virgin Mary, and he said to her, “My dear Lady, if you don't return the possessions of these people, who all came to observe your feast, then I won’t come again to this place. And I won’t serve your sanctuary.”</p>\n\n<p>While he was saying this, the priests heard a loud sound of knocking at the door. They rushed to find out what was happening. Behold, the Arabs who had stolen the people’s possessions were yelling, “Open the gates for us!”</p>\n\n<p>After the priests opened the gate, the Arabs came up to the priests, who [then] heard their report about all the possessions they had carried away. Upon seeing this [return of their possessions], the priests marveled and were amazed.</p>\n\n<p>They asked the Arabs [what had happened], and the Arabs told them everything that had befallen them. [They reported] how their eyes were blinded, how they were unable to move their feet, and how they heard a voice from the wind saying, “If you don’t return the possessions of all the people who have come for my feast, your eyes won’t see and your feet won't move. And a light will shine against you, and the city's judge will see you and condemn you for theft and robbery. Had I not remembered your previous service to my church, I would have destroyed you.”</p>\n\n<p>[The Arabs continued their report:] “When we heard this voice, we yelled out to you and knocked at the door. Behold, we have all your possessions with us.”</p>\n\n<p>After the people had heard this, the men and women rushed down from [the roof] above the upper room to take their garments and adornments. They [then] went to the icon with great joy, saying, “Rejoice, O Fullness of grace. Rejoice, O you who pour out joy. Rejoice, God is with you.” Each one of them bowed down to her as much as they were able.</p>\n\n<p>They asked her about the Arabs being saved, their eyes being opened, and their [feet] walking.</p>\n\n<p>Those Arabs came in front of the icon and bowed down while praising Our Lady, the Holy Virgin Mary, and they remained serving her until the day of their death. They reported her miracle to all the Muslims.</p>\n\n<p>May the blessings of her prayer be with her servant [King] Lebna Dengel forever and ever, amen.</p>"
      }
    ]
