    "title": "The priest Mark's wife, from Mallawi in Egypt, who is cured of a leprous sore on her belly by the prayers of Patriarch Matthew",
    "title_amharic": "በግብፅ ሀገር ማላዊ ከሚባል ስፍራ የሆነው ቄስ ማርቆስ ሚስት በሆዷ ላይ ከወጣባት የቆዳ በሽታ በፓትርያርክ ማቴዎስ ተፈወሰች።",
    "incipit": "ተአምር፡ ዘተከሥተት፡ በእደ፡ አቡነ፡ ሊቀ፡ ጳጳሳት፡ አባ፡ ማቴዎስ። ወሀሎ፡ ቀሲስ፡ እምሰብአ፡ መላዌ፡ ዘስሙ፡ ማርቆስ፡ ወቦቱ፡ ብእሲት፡ ወወፅአ፡ ላዕሌሃ፡ ለምጽ፡ ዲበ፡ ሕንብርታ፡ መጠነ፡ ክበበ፡ ኅብስት፡ ንኡስ።",
    "manuscript_count": 95,
    "most_read": false,
    "translations": [
      {
        "author": "Jeremy Brown with Ekaterina Pukhovaia",
        "text": "<p>A miracle performed by Our Lady Mary, Holy Twofold Virgin, the Mother of God, may her prayers and her intercession be with her servant [King] Lebna Dengel forever and ever amen.</p>\n\n<p>A miracle that was revealed through Patriarch Abba Matthew.</p>\n\n<p>There was a priest from the people of Mallawi called Mark. He had a wife, who developed a leprous sore on her stomach about the size of a small loaf of bread.</p>\n\n<p>The people of the city said to the priest, “Why do you sleep with your wife while she has leprosy and then perform the Eucharist? How could this possibly happen, if it is unclean and forbidden according to canon law?”</p>\n\n<p>Immediately, the priest got up, took his wife, and went to [Patriarch] Abba Matthew.</p>\n\n<p>Mark said to him, “Look, this is my wife, your servant. She got leprosy on her stomach. Your holy prayer indicated it to me, and from the moment I understood, I did not come close to her. So now I brought her to you so that you can heal her by your prayer.”</p>\n\n<p>Abba Matthew said to him, “My dear son, do you hold hatred against your wife? Have you lied about her because of this? You have said, ‘Leprosy has come upon her.’”</p>\n\n<p>Mark answered, “Dear Abba, I do not have any hatred toward her; rather, I love her like myself. Truly, it is because of the leprosy that is upon her that I have spoken to you. If you do not believe me, look with your own eyes at that spot after you open her clothes.”</p>\n\n<p>The patriarch said to him, “Stand, you and your wife, in front of the icon of Our Lady Mary, the Pure Virgin. She will reveal to me if there is leprosy upon her. You must also say the ‘Our Father who art in heaven.’”</p>\n\n<p>Immediately, they did just as he had commanded them. The patriarch stood together with him in front of the icon. He stretched out his hands and asked, “My dear Lady, Mother of Mercy, heal this woman.”</p>\n\n<p>Then he dipped his fingers in the oil of the candle that was burning in front of the icon. He laid his hands on the clothes of that woman, near the embroidered hem of her shirt. He anointed the place of the leprosy saying, “My dear Lady, Mother of Life, reveal to me righteousness in this priest who lied about his wife.”</p>\n\n<p>Then the patriarch said to the woman, “Uncover your stomach so that your husband can see it. He will show me the place of your leprosy.”</p>\n\n<p>Abba Matthew said this because he knew that the woman was purified from her leprosy by the prayer of Our Lady Mary.</p>\n\n<p>He [earlier] also had said to the husband, “You lied about your wife’s leprosy,” so that it would not be boasting when he healed her.</p>\n\n<p>Then the husband looked, but he did not see any leprosy on her. He said to Abba Matthew, “Dear father, look at the place on her body where the leprosy came out. So now she is cleansed. And if you do not believe me, ask her, because the leprosy was on her, and she would not deny you.”</p>\n\n<p>Abba Matthew said to the man, “You lied about your wife when you showed hate [against] her.”</p>\n\n<p>Then the man took his wife and departed from that place, marveling at God, worshiping him, and declaring the greatness of Our Lady Mary. He told all the people that the leprosy of his wife had been healed by the hand of Patriarch Abba Matthew.</p>\n\n<p>May the blessings of her prayer be with her servant [King] Lebna Dengel forever and ever, amen.</p>"
      }
    ]
