    "translations": [
      {
        "author": "Wallis Budge",
        "text": "<p>There was a certain transgressor of the God’s law who he had not one good deed [to his credit].</p>\n\n<p>One day he went on a journey. A sickness seized him, and he became helpless.</p>\n\n<p>His family said to him, “Give us some of your money and we will go to a physician [or magician].”</p>\n\n<p>The physician said to him, “Bring carob and oil.”</p>\n\n<p>The man gave the physician whatever he asked for, and his money came to an end.</p>\n\n<p>The sick man said to his wife, “Celebrate the commemoration of the Virgin Mary, and she will save me.” Having said this, he fell asleep.</p>\n\n<p>Our Lady Mary appeared to him in a vision and said, “You are a man who has lived all the days of your life without knowing me, but when death comes, then you claim to know me.”</p>\n\n<p>The sick man said, “Now I know [you], and I will become your servant. Don’t make me prepare for the final Judgement; heal me.”</p>\n\n<p>Our Lady Mary, who shows grace to all creatures, heals the sick, and is compassionate to all who take refuge with her, anointed the sick man’s whole body with her spittle.</p>\n\n<p>Straightaway he was healed.</p>\n\n<p>All those who saw and heard of this miracle marveled, and the man became pleasing to Our Lady Mary and loved her.</p>"
      }
    ]
