    "title": "A man who wanted to give a banquet on the Virgin Mary's feast but was unable because of a famine.",
    "title_amharic": "በረኀብ የተነሣ በድንግል ማርያም በዓል ቀን መደገስ ያቃተው ሰው።",
    "incipit": "ተብህለ፡ ከመ፡ ሀሎ፡ ፩ብእሲ፡ ዘያፈቅራ፡ ለእግዝእትነ፡ ቅድስት፡ ድንግል፡ በ፪ኤ፡ ማርያም፡ ማሪሃም፡ ወይገብር፡ ተዝካራ፡ በኵሉ፡ በዓላተ፡ እግዝእትነ፡ ቅድስት፡ ድንግል፡ በ፪ኤ፡ ማርያም፡ ማሪሃም፡ ወበጽሐ፡ ዐባር፡ ወአሐተ፡ ዕለተ፡ በበዓለ፡ እግዝእትነ፡ ቅድስት፡ ድንግል፡ በ፪ኤ፡ ማርያም፡ ማሪሃም፡ አልቦ፡ ዘይሁቦሙ፡ ኅብስተ፡ ወአጽዋዐ፡ ወኢምንተኒ።",
    "manuscript_count": 74,
    "most_read": false,
    "translations": [
      {
        "author": "Jeremy Brown with Ekaterina Pukhovaia",
        "text": "<p>A miracle performed by Our Lady Mary Mariham, the Holy Virgin, the Mother of God. May her intercession be with us, amen.</p>\n\n<p>A man who loved Our Lady Mary Mariham, the Holy Virgin, performed her remembrance on every feast of Our Lady Mary Mariham, the Holy Virgin. But a drought came on one of the feast days of Our Lady Mary Mariham, the Holy Virgin. This man was unable to offer the poor any bread, nor [could he offer them] the chalice.</p>\n\n<p>At once, this man told the people of his house to bring a little bit of honey from their supplies and to mix it with water. Then they brought the honey and mixed it with water.</p>\n\n<p>Our Lady Mary Mariham, the Holy Virgin, came to that man. She said to him, “Dear man, why are you grieving?”</p>\n\n<p>He answered, “I am upset about the love of Our Lady Mary Mariham, the Holy Virgin, and about her remembrance, because I do not have anything to offer.”</p>\n\n<p>Our Lady Mary Mariham, the Holy Virgin, replied, “I will give you anything that you want. Just as you love me, I love you.”</p>\n\n<p>Having said this, she disappeared from his sight.</p>\n\n<p>When that man returned to his home, he found his wife sitting outside. He said to her, “What did you see?”</p>\n\n<p>She said, “I saw Our Lady Mary Mariham, the Holy Virgin. And I begged her.”</p>\n\n<p>The man said to his wife, “Let’s go inside the house.”</p>\n\n<p>Then they entered their home and found baked fish and a set table. Everyone who saw this miracle and heard about it rejoiced and worshiped the glorious God and praised Our Lady Mary Mariham, the Holy Virgin. They gave a tithe to Our Lady Mary Mariham, the Holy Virgin and also everything they had in their house. They told the clergy everything Our Lady Mary Mariham, the Holy Virgin, had done for them.</p>\n\n<p>May her prayer and her blessing be with her servant forever and ever, amen.</p>"
      }
    ]
