    "title": "Book of Ledata la-Maryam: Part 02: Temple Jesus: The Virgin Mary and Joseph takes baby Jesus to the Temple and the virgins there see that he is the Messiah",
    "title_amharic": "መጽሐፈ ልደታ ለማርያም፤ አዲስ፤ ክፍል 02፤ ኢየሱስ በቤተመቅደስ፤ ድንግል ማርያም ሕፃኑን ኢየሱስን ወደ ቤተ መቅደስ ወሰደችው፤ በዚያ የነበሩ ደናግልም መሢሑ እርሱ እንደሆነ ዐወቁ። (ከ 1118 ጋር ተመሳሳይ?)",
    "incipit": "ወእምዝ፡ ወሰዳ፡ ኢየሩሳሌም፡ ወሕፃን፡ ምስሌሃ፡ ወቦኡ፡ ውስተ፡ መቅደስ፡ ከመዝ፡ ግበሩ፡ ላዕሌሁ፡ በከመ፡ ሕግ፨ ወሀሎ፡ ፩ብእሲ፡ በኢየሩሳሌም፡ ዘስሙ፡ ስምዖን፡ ነቢይ፡ ወጻድቅ፡ ዘረሥዓ፡ መዋዕሊሁ፡ ፈድፋደ፨ ወአስተርአዮ፡ መንፈስ፡ ቅዱስ፡ ከመ፡ ኢይፍልስ፡ እምዓለም፨…",
    "manuscript_count": 2,
    "most_read": false,
    "translations": [
      {
        "author": "Mehari Worku with Wendy Laura Belcher",
        "text": "<p>After this, Joseph took Mary and the child to Jerusalem, where they entered the Temple and performed what was required by the Law.</p>\n\n<p>A man in Jerusalem named Simon was a prophet and a righteous man. His age was so great that he had forgotten how old he was.</p>\n\n<p>The Holy Spirit had revealed to Simon that he would not pass from this world until he saw [the Messiah,] Christ Our Lord, born from the Virgin.</p>\n\n<p>[After many years,] the Holy Spirit took Simon to the Temple, where he saw the Holy Virgin and the child in her lap.</p>\n\n<p>Simon took the child from her and held him in his arms, blessing God.</p>\n\n<p>Simon said [to God], “Now, let your servant go in peace, according to your command.</p>\n\n<p>“My eyes have seen your salvation,</p>\n\n<p>“Which you have prepared for all your people to see</p>\n\n<p>“To reveal the light to the nations and</p>\n\n<p>“The glory to your people Israel.”</p>\n\n<p>When Joseph heard this [prayer,] his heart was strengthened.</p>\n\n<p>[Meanwhile,] the prophetess Anna was there, serving [in the Temple] with the other widows and the Virgin.</p>\n\n<p>The widows saw the child in her lap, not even two years after Mary had left them, and they rejoiced with her for they respected her because of her generosity and purity.</p>\n\n<p>Hearing what Simon had said [about the child,] they were amazed and believed that this child was the Christ who had come to the world to save humanity. Also, they believed that Mary was the Virgin about whom Isaiah prophesied.</p>\n\n<p>After this, Joseph, Mary, and the child returned to their town.</p>\n\n<p>May her prayers, blessings, and the mercy of her son. be with her servant Gabra Maryam, forever and ever. Amen!</p>"
      }
    ]
