    "title_amharic": "የ16ኛው ክፍለ ዘመን ኢትዮጵያዊ ንጉሥ ልብነ ድንግል (ዳግማዊ ዳዊት) በድንግል ማርያም ተጎበኘ፤ የወደፊት ዕጣ ፈንታውም ተነገረው፤ ክፍል 3",
    "incipit": "ወአመ ፡  ተኃጥአ ፡  ቦቱ ፡  ራእዩ ፡  እንተ ፡  ይሰምዕ ፡  ጊዜ ፡  መንፈቀ ፡  ሌሊት። እምግርማ ፡  ቃሉ ፡  ለመልአከ ፡  እግዚአብሔር ፡  ቅዱስ ፡  ራጉኤል ፡  ዘያደነግፅ ፡  ኀዘነ ፡  ወተከዘ ፡  ጥቀ ፡  ልብነ ፡  ድንግል ፡  ንጉሥ ፡  አኮኑ ፡  ደንገፀ ፡  ልቡናሁ። ወበእንተዝ ፡  ጸለየ ፡  በስብሐት ፡  ወበውዳሴ ፡  እንዘ ፡  ይብል ፡  አርእዪኒ ፡  ፍጹመ ፡  ዘወጠንኪ ፡  በቃለ ፡  መልአኩ ፡  ለወልድኪ ፡  ኦ እግዝእትየ ፡   ማርያም ፡  ፍቅርተ ፡  አቡየ ፡",
    "manuscript_count": 1,
    "most_read": false,
    "translations": [
      {
        "author": "Mehari Worku",
        "text": "<p>The miracle of Our Lady Mary, Holy Twofold Virgin, the Mother of God. May her prayer and blessings be with us forever and ever. Amen.</p>\n\n<p>When the terrifying vision of the Lord’s angel, Ragu‘el, which Lebna Dengel was seeing [since] midnight, disappeared, Lebna Dengel became very sad.</p>\n\n<p>As a result, he prayed to Mary in praise and gratitude, saying, “My dear generous Lady Mary, my father’s beloved, show me the end for what you have begun to show me through the word of your son’s angel. I beseech you in your son’s passion!”</p>\n\n<p>While he was praying at night in the angelic praise and intercession, he fell asleep for a short time.</p>\n\n<p>Then archangel Ragu‘el came and said, “Peace to you, king! [Due to your repentance,] today you have become [God’s] chosen one. Yesterday, however, you were a wicked-hearted [man].</p>\n\n<p>When the archangel said this to him, Lebna Dengel became terrified. For the angel’s voice was terrifying. [The archangel said,] “Don’t be afraid of me. The Lord has forgiven you due to his mother’s prayer [for you]. Listen to what I tell you [and] write to you, as [I did] yesterday.”</p>\n\n<p>The archangel [began] writing on the silk curtain: “As I told you yesterday, for two hundred fifty years there will be many Muslims in Shawa, at Yarar’s and Zeq̣wala foothill, in Katata, Mugar, Waggeda, Sehega, up to Geyon, Suhal, Tagulat, and Wifat, except Manzh. For the archangel Uriel, who received in a luminous chalice the pure blood—the cleanser of humanity from its sin—from Christ’s body, guards that place [i.e., Manzh].</p>\n\n<p>“You ancestors, the righteous kings, gave Manzh to the archangel Uriel. They did not cross River Lebanon.</p>\n\n<p>“Regarding that town whose name’s symbol is 'Ǝ, as I already mentioned to you, the holy God guards it from the Muslims through my hands until a peaceful and just king comes.</p>\n\n<p>“The symbol of his name in the Homily of the Words [of the?] Mother as Ze, 'Ǝ. The symbol of his scepter is Ze. His faith is from among the Jacobites, the children of Dioscorus, the Alexandrian Patriarch.</p>\n\n<p>“The children of Mina will be exiled from Shawa to the southwestern land. They will build their town in the land of Go.</p>\n\n<p>“That town is found near water, which is named River of Wine.</p>\n\n<p>“The children of Ya will be exiled to 'Ena‘ert. During the time of tribulation, when Mi’s children were going to Go, some of them would be cut off from the rest and flee to Gurage.</p>\n\n<p>“They will live among unbelievers in sadness due to lack of priests, except the very few left here and there as signs [of the priesthood].</p>\n\n<p>“However, [those who are] in Manzh, Malza, Waggeda, and Segahe will survive hiding in caves, cliffs, pits, ridges, and islands. God will hide them so that they confess Christianity to the coming Christian generation, whom Our God has chosen.</p>\n\n<p>“From Ya’s children in Manzh a king will [rise], according to Our God’s will. For that son of Ya loves the archangel Uriel.</p>\n\n<p>“Therefore, beseech Our God so that he might not extinguish the descendants of [Ya’s son]. [If you do this,] through our father Takla Haymanot’s prayers Ya’s son will have children who will rule part of Shawa surrounded by unbelievers, the ‘Adal [Sultanate], and Muslims. Ya’s son will guard Takla Haymanot’s tomb until the age of Muslims is completed.</p>\n\n<p>“Dabra Asbo will never have a calm season until the king who will be king after the two hundred fifty years [of] Muslims [dominance], which I told you before.”</p>\n\n<p>After saying this, the archangel Ragu‘el disappeared from him. Lebna Dengel remained with sadness and mourning.</p>\n\n<p>May her prayers and blessings be with us forever and ever. Amen.</p>"
      }
    ]
