    "title_amharic": "የ16ኛው ክፍለ ዘመን ኢትዮጵያዊ ንጉሥ ልብነ ድንግል (ዳግማዊ ዳዊት) በድንግል ማርያም ተጎበኘ፤ የወደፊት ዕጣ ፈንታውም ተነገረው፤ ክፍል 4",
    "incipit": "ወበአሐቲ ፡  እመዋዕል ፡  እንዘ ፡  ሀሎ ፡  ልብነ ፡  ድንግል ፡  ውስተ ፡  ኀዘን ፡  ክቡድ ፡  በይነ ፡  ዘይመጽእ ፡  ላዕሌሁ ፡  ይቤ ፡  በውዑይ ፡  ኅሊና ፡  እንከሰ ፡  አኀዝኩ ፡  እትናገር ፡  ምስለ ፡  እግዝእትየ ፡  እንተ ፡  ፆረት ፡  እሳተ ፡  መለኮት ፡  እንዘ ፡  መሬት ፡  ወሐመድ ፡  አነ።",
    "manuscript_count": 1,
    "most_read": false,
    "translations": [
      {
        "author": "Mehari Worku",
        "text": "<p>A miracle of Our Lady Mary, Holy Twofold Virgin, the Mother of God. May her prayer and blessings be with us forever and ever. Amen.</p>\n\n<p>One day, while Lebna Dengel was in deep sadness due to what was coming upon him, he said passionately, “Alas! While I am dust and ash, I began speaking with my Lady, who carried the divine fire.”</p>\n\n<p>He continued, “My dear Lady, the merciful, send me Ragu‘el your angel to tell me what is going to happen in my country in later days.”</p>\n\n<p>Immediately, the archangel Ragu‘el came down from heaven and appeared to Lebna Dengel in a dream and said to him, “What are you asking the Virgin Mary, the merciful and compassionate mother of Emmanuel Our God?”</p>\n\n<p>King Lebna Dengel replied in his dream to the angel St. Ragu‘el as if he was speaking with a friend.</p>\n\n<p>Then he said, “When is the Jacobite orthodox king coming? What is the sign of his birth? Is he going to be from Ya’s seed or king Mi’s descendants? Or will he from other kings?”</p>\n\n<p>The angel Ragu‘el wrote king Ya’s name on the [sanctuary’s] curtain, saying, “Listen to what I, according to the command from the merciful God’s mother, am telling you, and notice everything I write to you.</p>\n\n<p>“He is not from other kings. Rather, he is your descendant.</p>\n\n<p>“Mi’s descendants will settle in the land of Go, ruling over the southwestern land, [which is] Arab up to Mesewwa, [with] unbelievers and Muslims from the Sea of Enoch to the border of Arabia, save Gurage and Janjaro.</p>\n\n<p>“The town of ‘Anar‘et will remain confessing Christianity without baptism due to lack of priests during those two hundred fifty years of Muslim [dominance].</p>\n\n<p>“A beloved for the archangel Uriel will be born from Ya’s descendants and rule over half of Shawa for one hundred fifty years across nine generations. [During that time] it will be peaceful and safe.</p>\n\n<p>“Half of it will be ruled by Muslims for two hundred fifty years.</p>\n\n<p>“Mi’s children will rule over Go, the southwestern lands, and the southern lands. There will be one king whose reign will be the best.</p>\n\n<p>“During his reign, many churches will be built in the lands under his rule. He will follow the orthodox faith, which is from the Alexandrian patriarch, whose see is the tree of life and salvation.</p>\n\n<p>“As a result, Satan envies his children. A wicked king will come from the descendants of this peaceful king, who will be born from a wicked king and wicked people’s daughter.</p>\n\n<p>“Satan will drag him into a love of sorcery. Satan will make him inhale an unclean tree’s smoke [tobacco?]. The Lord will kill him quickly. Kingship will be lost from this king’s descendants.</p>\n\n<p>“A Muslim king, whose name is Qa ‘A, will rise in his time from this Muslim king who is chasing you from place to place and brought you to prayer.</p>\n\n<p>“As it is written in the Apocalypse of the righteous pillar of faith, the Egyptian Shenouda, ash will rain from heaven at this time[, the reign of Qa ‘A].</p>\n\n<p>“In the thirty-third year after ash rain from heaven, famine will come from God due to people’s lack of love for one another and [their lack of] veneration for God’s body and blood. Every year the Holy Spirit’s blessing will be diminishing among the sanctuary’s priests. For they[, the priests,] do not have a good shepherd who guards the Jacobite faith’s flock, which the pure Egyptian ewe gave birth to.</p>\n\n<p>“However, a Jacobite king will rise due to the prayers from anchorite monks of Hagara Maryam, who hate the unclean tree’s smoke.”</p>\n\n<p>After saying this, the archangel Ragu‘el disappeared from king Lebna Dengel. The king stayed where he was, glorifying the Lord and praising Our Lady Mary, Holy Twofold Virgin, the Mother of God, because she did not abandon him during his time of trials. Nevertheless, sadness was still holding on to him.</p>\n\n<p>May her prayer and blessings be with us forever and ever. Amen.</p>"
      }
    ]
