    "title_amharic": "መጽሐፈ ነገረ ማርያም፤ ወር C፤ ክፍል 01፤ ድንግል ማርያም የገዳቤሪያ ክፉ ሰዎች ሲዖል እንዲገቡ ፈረደችባቸው፤ በዚያም ለሁለት ወራት አቆየቻቸው።",
    "incipit": "ወሶበ፡ ተፈጸሙ፡ እሉ፡ ቃላት፡ እምአፉሃ፡ ለእግዝእትነ፡ ... አስተርአያ፡ ለእግዝእትነ፡ ግብተ፡ ገብርኤል፡ መልአክ፨ ወይቤላ፡ አሜን፡ አሜን፡ ለይኵን፡ ለይኩን፡ ወኵሎ፡ ዘሀለይኪ፡ ንግበር፡ ለኪ፨ ወዘንተ፡ ብሂሎ፡ ዓርገ፡ ውስተ፡ ሰማያት፨ ወሖረት፡ እግዝእትነ፡ ማርያም፡ ፍኖታ፡ ወበጽሐት፡ ኀበ፡ ሀገረ፡ ገዳቤርያ፡…",
    "manuscript_count": 1,
    "most_read": false,
    "translations": [
      {
        "author": "Mehari Worku with Wendy Laura Belcher",
        "text": "<p>When Our Lady Mary, the Holy Two-Fold Virgin, finished saying these words, the Angel Gabriel appeared to her suddenly and said, “Amen! Amen! Let it be! Let it be! We will do whatever you think [we should do].”</p>\n\n<p>Having said this, he returned to heaven.</p>\n\n<p>Our Lady Mary continued on her way and reached the city of Gedabierya and [its] wicked people. They were idolaters who had no fear of the Lord. Sinfully, men slept with men and women slept with women. They ate dead carcasses, torn-up animals, and blood. Our Lady sat at the gate of their city and saw their sins clearly.</p>\n\n<p>She exclaimed to Joseph, “Are these animals or humans?”</p>\n\n<p>Joseph replied, “Are you noticing what Satan has done to the Lord’s creations? He made them like animals who lack intelligence.”</p>\n\n<p>Our Lady Mary said, “Do you want me to drown them in the abyss of Sheol?”</p>\n\n<p>Joseph replied, “’Kind people will be saved by their kindness.’ It’s right for you to be merciful to these people.”</p>\n\n<p>That night, she stayed there [at the gate] eating and drinking nothing.</p>\n\n<p>At midnight, the Lord sent the angel of death with many angels of darkness. The angels angrily and hastily yanked out the souls [of the Gedabierya people and left their bodies behind]. None of the city’s people were spared, whether male or female, for the Lord was enthroned in his wrath. The abyss of darkness took them.</p>\n\n<p>In the morning, when Our Lady Mary and Joseph woke up from their sleep, they couldn’t hear any human sounds.</p>\n\n<p>Our Lady Mary asked Joseph, “Do you know what happened to them?”</p>\n\n<p>Joseph set off to look for the city’s people but found the gates shut. He opened them and entered into the city. He found [all] the people dead in their beds: men and women, old people and children.</p>\n\n<p>He clapped his hands, whistled [with amazement], and returned to Our Lady Mary, where he told her everything [he saw].</p>\n\n<p>Our Lady replied, “They truly deserved it!”</p>\n\n<p>She stayed there for three days and was ready to leave.</p>\n\n<p>Joseph asked, “My dear Lady, who is going to bury the city’s people?”</p>\n\n<p>Our Lady replied, “I don’t know. Who buries wolves and hyenas?”</p>\n\n<p>Joseph said, “If we had not come to their city, they would have been better off. This punishment wouldn’t have come upon them. They died because of us. Now, have mercy on them so that their deaths won’t be counted as a sin against us by the Lord.”</p>\n\n<p>Our Lady Mary replied, “If we are going to help them, wait [a little]. Let them be punished for awhile, so that they might experience the place of adulterers and polluted ones [suffering].”</p>\n\n<p>They stayed there for two months.</p>\n\n<p>Then, Mary stood up, turned her face to the east, stretched out her hand, and called out, “Dieriedu’ Gbtomr Dieradies Ysebaiel. Ammanuel, listen to me about these people who are sleeping in their houses: you should return their souls to their bodies. Yes, Lord, I beseech you, remove evil thoughts from them and [all] unclean and perverted spirits. Yes, Lord, I beseech you, for you came down from the highest heaven and became human from me.</p>\n\n<p>You were born from me, according to your will, without sin. Yes, I beseech you, my dear son, my beloved, and my king. Do not despise the request of your ma[id]...”</p>\n\n<p>…</p>\n\n<p>All the blind saw, the mute spoke, and the deaf heard. The lepers became clean. The demons were cast out. When the people saw [all] this, they marveled.</p>\n\n<p>The person who wrote this book, may the Lord write his name in the heavenly kingdom. Amen.</p>\n\n<p>May her prayer, blessing and the mercy of her son be with her servant Gabra Maryam, forever and ever. Amen.</p>"
      }
    ]
