    "title_amharic": "መጽሐፈ ፍልሰታ ለማርያም፤ አዲስ2፤ ዕረፍታ፤ ሲዖል፤ ኢየሱስ ለድንግል ማርያም ገሃነምን (ሲዖልን) አስጎበኛት።",
    "incipit": "ወበአሐቲ፡ ዕለት፡ አንሥአት፡ እግዝእትነ፡ ቅድስት፡ ድንግል፡ በ፪ማርያም፡ ወላዲተ፡ አምላክ፡ አዕይንቲሃ፡ ወነጸረት፡ ማኅደረ፡ እለ፡ አልቦሙ፡ ኁልቍ፡ ወእሙንቱሰ፡ ይበርሁ፡ ፈድፋደ፡ ወይወፅእ፡ በህየ፡ ፄና፡ ዕጣን፡ ዘመዓዛሁ፡ ሠናይ፡ ወይሰማዕ፡ ድምፀ፡ ቃለ፡ ቀርን፡ በውስተ፡ እሉ፡ ማኅደራት፡ ወብዙኃን፡ እድ፡ ወአንስት፡ ይቀውሙ፡ ውስቴቶን። ወእምዝ፡ ትቤሎ፡ እግዝእትነ፡ ማርያም፡ ለእግዚእነ፡ እግዚእየ፡ ወአምላኪየ፡ እለ፡ መኑ፡ እሙንቱ፡ እለ፡ ይነብሩ፡ ውስተዝ፡ ማኅደር።",
    "manuscript_count": 1,
    "most_read": false,
    "translations": [
      {
        "author": "Mehari Worku with Wendy Laura Belcher",
        "text": "<p>One day [in heaven], Our Lady Mary, the Two-fold Virgin Mother of God, saw countless places that glowed with great light, that emitted the sweet aroma of good incense, and that sounded with trumpets. Many men and women were standing inside those glowing places.</p>\n\n<p>After [seeing all] this, Our Lady Mary, the Two-fold Virgin Mother of God said to Our Lord, “My Lord and my God, who are these people who live in that place?”</p>\n\n<p>Our Lord replied, “Those are the righteous and generous people. Behold, the light is shining on them because of their greatness. They are expecting joy and gladness on the Last Day.”</p>\n\n<p>Then, Mary looked [down] at a dark city, from which a noisome smelling smoke floated, due to the great fire burning inside it. Many people were standing and crying in that city.</p>\n\n<p>Our Lady Mary, the Two-fold Virgin Mother of God said to Our Lord, “Tell me, who are those standing in the dark city?”</p>\n\n<p>Our Lord replied, “That is the city of Gehanna. Those who are standing in it are sinners waiting the judgment prepared for them. All of those who refuse my commandments will be put in this fire.”</p>\n\n<p>Then, Our Lady Mary, the Two-fold Virgin Mother of God, heard the words of the generous people [in the glowing place], who said, “Glory to you, my Lord Jesus Christ who gives much [in reward] for [even a] little [righteousness] to those who call upon you and believe in you.”</p>\n\n<p>When Our Lady Mary, the Two-fold Virgin Mother of God, the Compassionate of Mind, heard the words of the generous people, she rejoiced.</p>\n\n<p>But, then she heard the crying and wailing of the sinners standing in the darkness. They said, “Jesus Christ, the Son of God, when you come to judge the living and the dead, have mercy on us and forgive us!”</p>\n\n<p>When the Mother of Mercy heard this, she became terribly sad. She [turned to her son and] said, “My Lord and my God, have mercy on the sinners. Don’t despise your handiwork when you come to judge them. For I have heard their groaning and weeping and I have become sad for them.”</p>\n\n<p>Our Lord said to his mother, “O my mother, you are beatified and blessed. Anyone who calls upon your name and commemorates you will be saved from oppression.”</p>\n\n<p>Our Lady replied to her beloved son, “My Lord and my God, [let it be] according to your holy Father’s word and your saving and holy word. For everything you promised me on earth has been given to me since you are Christ, who was born from me in the end times according to your will for the salvation of Adam and his children.”</p>\n\n<p>May He also save us from the snare of the enemy by the prayer of Our Lady Mary, the Two-fold Virgin Mother of God, forever and ever. Amen.</p>"
      }
    ]
